{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_003","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.","location_hint":"paragraph 73","char_start":1504,"char_end":1575,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_004","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"In this guide, we will introduce the system requirements for installing ComfyUI. Due to frequent updates of ComfyUI, this document may not be updated in a timely manner. Please refer to the relevant instructions in ComfyUI .\nRegardless of which version of ComfyUI you use, it runs in a separate Python environment.","location_hint":"paragraph 74","char_start":1577,"char_end":1891,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_005","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"Currently, we support the following operating systems:","location_hint":"paragraph 77","char_start":1921,"char_end":1975,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_006","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"macOS (supports Apple Silicon, such as the M series)","location_hint":"paragraph 80","char_start":1994,"char_end":2046,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_007","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"You can refer to the following sections to learn about the installation methods for different systems and versions of ComfyUI. In the installation of different versions, we have simply described the system requirements.","location_hint":"paragraph 81","char_start":2049,"char_end":2268,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_008","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"ComfyUI Desktop currently supports standalone installation for Windows and MacOS (ARM) , currently in Beta","location_hint":"paragraph 83","char_start":2293,"char_end":2399,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a8c5d541c698_009","source_id":"src_a8c5d541c698","source_hash":"ee1e14bc82ad9ec2a763a7ed0bf487fe4802b73cc38069a27a1954b5b4d223af","text":"Because Desktop is always built based on the stable release , so the latest updates may take some time to experience for Desktop, if you want to always experience the latest version, please use the portable version or manual installation","location_hint":"paragraph 85","char_start":2436,"char_end":2673,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T05:23:53.303Z"}
